# Pi {version} — upstream source and bundle layout

This Debian package repackages Pi's official standalone Linux bundle. The
package contains upstream program and resource files, not a source archive.
These version-pinned references identify the upstream source; they do not
assert source closure or make a compliance determination.

## Upstream source

- Release tag: `{tag}`
- Source tree: <https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/tree/{tag}>
- Source archive: <https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/archive/refs/tags/{tag}.tar.gz>
- Official standalone bundle: the `pi-linux-x64.tar.gz` and
  `pi-linux-arm64.tar.gz` assets of the `{tag}` release.

## Installed layout

The complete upstream bundle root is installed under `/usr/lib/pi`, so the
executable's own directory is also the package resource directory that Pi
resolves themes, assets, export templates, documentation, and examples from.
`/usr/bin/pi` is the package launcher. Pi itself is updated only through APT;
the launcher points `PI_SELF_UPDATE_COMMAND` at the packaged
`/usr/lib/pi/apt-update` helper, which refuses to modify the installation and
prints the APT command instead.
